{
  "$schema": "../../schemas/ship.schema.json",
  "id": "fer-de-lance",
  "name": "Fer-de-lance",
  "concept": true,
  "manufacturer": "Zorgon Petterson",
  "role": "multirole",
  "description": "The most talked-about hull in the galaxy: a private hotel with a fighter's bones. Nearly two and a half times the length of a Cobra, a glass deck along its spine, and barbs swept back from its shoulders like the head of a lance. Zorgon Petterson say it is for people who never ask the price. Everyone else is already saving.",
  "credits": {
    "authors": ["Witchspace contributors"],
    "license": "CC-BY-SA-4.0",
    "aiAssisted": true,
    "notes": "Original Witchspace geometry: a lance-head hull, one hexagon scaled along its length so every panel is flat, swelling to a shoulder, with two barbs swept back past the tail. A nod to the 1984 name; its size, hold and character come from Samuel Penn's Ships of Elite for Mongoose Traveller (CC BY-SA 4.0). Nothing traced. Built by Zorgon Petterson, the 1984 maker's name kept as homage."
  },
